{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With only one data point (config_010: multimodal, scgpt+resnet50, transformer, concat → 47.1% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion is actually contributing or whether one modality dominates. Config_001 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scgpt, transformer) is the cleanest single-modality baseline matching the RNA side of config_010 exactly. If RNA-only approaches 47%, the image modality adds little value and future effort should focus on RNA encoder/aggregation improvements. If RNA-only is substantially lower, image is critical and we should prioritize image encoder and fusion strategy experiments. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most fundamental architectural question (is multimodal worth it?) before committing remaining budget to specific improvements."
}

